  "body": "Stacked on #1330. This branch starts from the head of #1330 (`58df4b729`, fork branch `mkinney:issue/1198-drag-to-move`) with `origin/main` merged in. Until #1330 merges, the diff shows the commits of #1330 too. The new work is commit `043b7e0a9`.\n\n## What changed\n- The viewport bar has a new Rotate button after Move. Move and Rotate are mutually exclusive. A toggle cancels the live drag of the other mode.\n- With Rotate on, the one selected part shows three rings round its bounding-box centre. Each ring is square to one shown axis. The ring radius is a constant 60 px on the screen. A press within 6 px of a ring grabs the nearest ring.\n- The drag angle is the point where the cursor ray meets the ring plane, measured about the centre. The angle is unwrapped, so a drag can go past 180 degrees. During the drag the part preview turns and the bar shows `Turn about Z: +35.0°`. The world does not change during the drag.\n- The release queues one `CommandKind::TurnModelBy { name, axis, angle_rad }`. The drain runs the existing `MoveModel`, so the turn is one undo step. The generated operations go stale and the stock follows the part, as for a typed turn.\n- An aligned setup turns the part about the axis that the user sees (the turn goes back through the setup alignment).\n- Escape cancels the turn with no history step. A turn that ends at its start angle queues nothing and writes no rotation noise (#2177).\n- A bad axis, a non-finite angle or a missing part is refused by name on the status line.\n- New files: `crates/ui/src/turn_drag.rs` (the drag law), `crates/ui/src/egui_app/turn_handles.rs` (the paint), `crates/ui/src/egui_app/viewport_bar_tests.rs` (the bar tests moved out to keep `viewport_bar.rs` near 400 lines).\n- No new app command, so no new MCP tool. MCP `move_model` already sets the rotation.\n\n## How the stale path is pinned\n`body_turn::a_ring_drag_is_one_undoable_turn_that_stales_the_path_and_carries_the_stock` drags the Z ring on the seeded document. Before the drag, `camcraft_app::posting::program_ops` returns `Ok`. After the release, it returns an `Err` that contains \"regenerate\", so the post refuses. One undo makes the history clean again and `program_ops` returns `Ok` again. The same test checks that the stock box still holds the turned part. The app-level pin `crates/app/tests/commands_undo.rs::a_moved_part_marks_generated_ops_stale_and_undo_clears_it` already covers a pure rotation in the stale stamp.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `egui_app::tests::body_turn::*` (5 tests): rings only in Rotate mode at a constant size; one undoable turn that makes the path stale and carries the stock; Escape cancels; a zero turn adds nothing; empty space still orbits.\n- `turn_drag_tests::*` (6 tests): the angle under the cursor, a drag past half a turn, no command for a press off the rings or a turn in place, the centre stays in place, a turned setup, refusals by name.\n- `egui_app::viewport_bar::tests::move_and_rotate_modes_never_share_the_part`.\n\n## Readings\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`) on head `043b7e0a9`: ui lib 954 passed, 1 failed; boundary, boundary_picks, feedback, fixtures, gpu_render, machine, models, operations, shell, sinker_setup, tap_hand, theme_files, waterjet_tool all green. The one failure is `stock_fit_controls_follow_the_selected_shape`, which also fails on main (#2170, fix PR #2171).\n- Clippy `-p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n- No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No hand test in the live window. The screenshots come from the kittest harness render of the shipping shell with the GPU viewport, at 1280x720.\n- No angle snapping (not asked for; see `docs/decisions/2047-drag-to-rotate.md`).\n- `shell.rs` was already longer than 400 lines before this change; this PR adds 11 lines to it.\n\n## Screenshots\nBefore (Move mode of #1330 on this branch: the move balls, no rings):\n![before move](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/c75bf71a4a9cb55f12442cdc2b6b5b8775178e51/pr-2047/before-move.png?raw=true)\nAfter (Rotate mode, a Z-ring drag of +35 degrees in progress):\n![after rotate](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/c75bf71a4a9cb55f12442cdc2b6b5b8775178e51/pr-2047/after-rotate.png?raw=true)\n\nChangelog: The viewport bar has a Rotate mode: drag a ring on the selected part to turn it about an axis through its centre, as one undo step.\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2047\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
